===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|plateau|lang=fr}}, diminutive of {{term|plat||a plate}}; see [[plate]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈplætəʊ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/plæˈtoʊ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-plateau.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* Homophones: [[plateaux#Pronunciation|plateaux]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|plateaus|plateaux}}

# A largely [[level]] [[expanse]] of [[land]] at a high [[elevation]]; [[tableland]].
# A comparatively [[stable]] level in something that [[varies]].
# {{context|dated|lang=en}} An [[ornamental]] [[dish]] for the table; a [[tray]] or [[salver]].
# {{context|sports|broadcasting|lang=en}} A notable level of attainment or achievement.

